## 3. Ground rules (user preferences)

- Work **one gap group at a time**: implement, test, then commit.
- For each group: push the grammar fork, bump `[grammars.raku].rev` in
  `extension.toml`, update `test/highlight.raku` + `highlights.scm` as needed,
  commit + push the extension repo.
- Never commit/push without being asked (except as part of an approved group
  workflow). Don't touch the dotfiles repo commit unless asked.
- Keep the grammar's own test suite failure set unchanged (see §5).

## 4. Grammar workflow (exact commands)

From `/home/johnm/Projects/tree-sitter-raku`:

```sh
# edit grammar.js and/or src/scanner.c
timeout 300 tree-sitter generate      # SLOW (~1-2 min); fix reported conflicts
timeout 280 tree-sitter test          # confirm failure set unchanged
# probe with small files:
printf 'sub f($a?) { }\n' > /tmp/one.raku && tree-sitter parse /tmp/one.raku

# commit (generated files are gitignored upstream -> force-add):
git add grammar.js src/scanner.c
git add -f src/parser.c src/node-types.json src/tree_sitter/parser.h \
           src/tree_sitter/array.h src/grammar.json
git commit -m "..."; git push origin HEAD:main
```

Then in `/home/johnm/Projects/zed-raku`:
- set `[grammars.raku].rev` in `extension.toml` to the new commit;
- update `languages/raku/highlights.scm` and `test/highlight.raku`;
- `git add -A && git commit && git push origin main`.

`scripts/build-grammar.sh` automates generate + push + rev bump (uses the SSH
alias and a small Python snippet to edit only the raku grammar's rev).

### tree-sitter gotchas

- The `externals: [...]` array order **must match** the enum order in
  `src/scanner.c` (e.g. `_regex_body` / `TOKEN_REGEX_BODY` were inserted just
  before `_ERROR` / `TOKEN_ERROR`).
- Add a `conflicts` entry **only** when `tree-sitter generate` explicitly asks
  for one; then re-run and remove any "unnecessary conflicts" it reports.
- `token.immediate(...)` is used to require adjacency (e.g. `%h{...}`,
  `.method`, twigils, `1..10`).
- Inlining internal rules (`inline: [...]`) made `parser.c` **larger** here —
  avoid it.
- String-literal query terms must exist as grammar tokens; unknown ones can
  silently mis-match.

## 5. Testing protocol

- Baseline: `tree-sitter test` → 199 parses, 172 successful, **27 pre-existing
  failures** (Perl-oriented corpus). Compare with:
  `tree-sitter test 2>&1 | grep '✗' | sed 's/\x1b\[[0-9;]*m//g' | sort`.
  Only "Slow parse rate" warnings may differ.
- `tree-sitter parse /home/johnm/Projects/zed-raku/test/highlight.raku` should
  report **0** errors.
- `raku -c /home/johnm/Projects/zed-raku/test/highlight.raku` → `Syntax OK`.
- Every query must compile:
  `tree-sitter query languages/raku/<q>.scm test/highlight.raku` for
  highlights, brackets, indents, outline, textobjects, injections, overrides.
- Run queries from the **grammar** dir (so it uses the local parser), not from
  the extension dir — running `tree-sitter query` on an unknown file type from
  the extension dir can make the CLI auto-clone grammars into
  `zed-raku/grammars/`.

## 6. Zed integration

- The installed dev extension is a **symlink** to `/home/johnm/Projects/zed-raku`,
  so editing the project updates the installed files; but grammar rev changes
  and query changes need a **rebuild**: Extensions page → **Raku** → **Rebuild**
  (or re-run `zed: install dev extension`).
- Zed's dev-extension builder checks out the grammar into
  `/home/johnm/Projects/zed-raku/grammars/` and compiles `raku.wasm` /
  `pod.wasm` there. **Do not delete that directory** — doing so caused
  `failed to load language Raku: No such file or directory` until the next
  rebuild.
- Debug: `zed: open log`, or relaunch with `zed-editor --foreground`.
- LSP: the extension resolves `raku-navigator` from PATH first, else the
  `lsp.raku-navigator.settings.path` setting. Zed settings already point at the
  PATH wrapper and set `includePaths`. The `raku-navigator` wrapper responds to
  an LSP `initialize` correctly.
- The settings file's `file_types` Perl mapping has the Raku suffixes commented
  out, so nothing competes for `.raku`/`.rakumod`.

